; Under -V --unround, a balance report's grand total adds the values -V
; gives the lots to the other amounts at full precision, so where they do
; not cancel exactly it shows the residue, on every run; without --unround
; it rounds to 0, as it always did.
;
; The first journal is 763.test's.  Ledger keeps the price of 1 BBB,
; bought at 2.653329339867 GBP, to six decimal places, as the lot's
; {GBP2.653329} and as BBB's market price, so -V values the lot at
; GBP2.653329 (printed GBP3, GBP showing no decimals) while the opening
; balance holds the cost as written, GBP-2.653329339867: the total is
; GBP-0.000000339867.  The euros cancel exactly.  The second journal is
; 964.test's: -V values its lots at their fixated prices, €208.00 at
; $1.3109 as $272.6672 and €4.16 at $1.2798689 as $5.324254624, against
; the $-277.99 of the other two postings, which leaves $0.001454624: the
; transaction balances only to the cent, and -B --unround shows the same
; residue, as it did in 3.4.1.  -p picks one journal per block.
;
; The residue is the full-precision sum of the valued lots and the other
; amounts.  Adding two amounts keeps only the left one's full-precision
; flag, and a lot's value is a new amount without it, so the sum kept the
; residue only when a part kept at full precision came first.  Ledger
; used to add the parts in an order that could change from one run to
; the next, and these totals printed 0 on most runs (3.4.1's on every
; run); a total now keeps full precision whenever one of its parts did,
; whichever is added first.
;
; Without --unround nothing in the total keeps full precision, so it
; prints at the commodities' display precision, as 0.  The opening
; balance prints all its digits either way, as an amount Ledger infers
; from a cost does when its commodity shows no decimals (#1692), but that
; does not carry into a sum.

2011-01-01 * Opening balance
    Assets:Investments           1 "BBB" @  2.653329339867 GBP
    Equity:Opening balance

2011-01-10 * Fee
    Liabilities:Credit Card                         -2.83 EUR
    Expenses:Fees                                 (2.83/2 EUR)
    Assets:Receivable

; The journal of 964.test.
2012/08/22 Payment
    Accrued                       €208.00  {=$1.3109}     @ $1.2798689
    Expenses                      €4.16    {=$1.2798689}  @ $1.2798689
    Assets                        $-271.54
    Income:Currency Conversion    $-6.45

test bal -V --unround --flat -p 2011
                GBP3  Assets:Investments
           1.415 EUR  Assets:Receivable
  GBP-2.653329339867  Equity:Opening balance
           1.415 EUR  Expenses:Fees
           -2.83 EUR  Liabilities:Credit Card
--------------------
  GBP-0.000000339867
end test

test bal -V --flat -p 2011
                GBP3  Assets:Investments
            1.42 EUR  Assets:Receivable
  GBP-2.653329339867  Equity:Opening balance
            1.42 EUR  Expenses:Fees
           -2.83 EUR  Liabilities:Credit Card
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal -V --unround --flat -p 2012
             $272.67  Accrued
            $-271.54  Assets
               $5.32  Expenses
              $-6.45  Income:Currency Conversion
--------------------
        $0.001454624
end test

test bal -V --flat -p 2012
             $272.67  Accrued
            $-271.54  Assets
               $5.32  Expenses
              $-6.45  Income:Currency Conversion
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal -B --unround --flat -p 2012
           $272.6672  Accrued
            $-271.54  Assets
        $5.324254624  Expenses
              $-6.45  Income:Currency Conversion
--------------------
        $0.001454624
end test
